q BT 65.20 771.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.997 Tw (Eddie Malone had driven Don Salvatore Romano for fifteen years, and in all that time the old) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 750.98 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (man had never once asked him to wait outside a warehouse at midnight.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 721.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.185 Tw (That was the thing Eddie could never forget about the night the Don died. Not the restaurant.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 701.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.228 Tw (Not the drive home. The warehouse. The Don had tapped twice on the glass between them --) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 680.68 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.348 Tw (two taps meant stop, no questions -- and Eddie had pulled into a dark lot off the highway, and a) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 660.27 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.385 Tw (man had gotten into the back seat, and the Don had said, "Drive," and for eleven minutes) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 639.86 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (nobody in that car said a single word.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 610.38 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.099 Tw (The next morning, Salvatore Romano was dead. A heart attack, the doctor said. Sixty-eight) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 589.98 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.209 Tw (years old, a bad heart, a lifetime of rich food and worry. The family buried him on a Friday, and) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 569.57 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.487 Tw (his son Nico took over the business on Monday, and Nico told everyone the same story: he had) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 549.16 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (been in Miami that night, a thousand miles away, closing a deal.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 519.68 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.976 Tw (Eddie never told anyone about the warehouse. Drivers who talk do not stay drivers. They stay) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 499.27 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.802 Tw (quiet, and they stay alive, and Eddie Malone had a wife and two daughters and a mortgage, so) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 478.86 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (he stayed quiet for fifteen years.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 449.38 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Then Nico sold the old car.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 419.90 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.001 Tw (It was a black sedan, older than Eddie's marriage, and the new owner's mechanic called Eddie) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 399.49 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.284 Tw (because something was rattling in the glovebox. Eddie went down to the lot on a Tuesday) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 379.08 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.731 Tw (afternoon, opened the glovebox the way he had opened it a thousand times, and found what) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 358.67 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (fifteen years of driving had hidden from him.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 329.19 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (A photograph. Creased. Faded. Tucked behind the car's manual, where no one ever looked.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 299.71 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.487 Tw (It showed the old Don, Salvatore Romano, standing beside his car on the night he died. He was) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 279.30 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.841 Tw (shaking hands with the man from the warehouse. And on the back, in the Don's own shaky) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 258.89 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (handwriting, were the words that stopped Eddie's heart:) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 229.41 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("If I die tonight, it was him.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 199.93 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.148 Tw (Eddie turned the photograph over and looked at the man's face again. He knew that face. He had) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 179.52 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.143 Tw (driven that face home from restaurants and airports and weddings for fifteen years. He had) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 159.11 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.801 Tw (watched that face cry at the old Don's funeral, standing beside the coffin in a black suit,) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 138.70 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (accepting condolences with tears in his eyes.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 109.22 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.216 Tw (The man in the photograph was Nico Romano. The Don's own son. The man who was supposed) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 88.81 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (to be in Miami.) Tj ET Q
